371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (We were sitting around after dinner last night when my wife says something along the lines of "Siggy is a complete bitcoin nut." She says this often in social situations, but it rarely spurs any conversation. My friend's wife said "what the hell is bitcoin, anyway?", and everyone turned to look at me. Even though I have been obsessed for more than 8 years now, I always struggle with this simple question. I blurted out some stuff about internet money, double spending, inflation proof, etc. I second guessed every word that came out of my mouth. None of it mattered anyway. They wanted to know how much a bitcoin cost when I first bought it, and how much it was worth now. They liked the answer. The wife wanted to know if it was hard to buy bitcoin. I mentioned cash app, and she said she uses it but didn't know you could buy bitcoin. I explained that it was easy to start buying on the app, but then I talked about NYKNYC and hardware wallets. They both were very interested, which surprised me.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (This morning they asked if I could help them make their first purchase on cash app. First my friend's wife bought some, then my friend downloaded the app.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (They had many more questions, so I suggested they read Lyn Alden's book Broken Money.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
